	2. Container orchestration
		2.1 As all technologies/products do, containers also require a way to be managed.
		2.2 And this is done with container orchestration, introducing the ability to scale up, down, load balance, centrally manage and track the containers.
	3. Kubernetes architecture
		3.1 Node: Physical or virtual machine where the kubernetes is installed
		3.2 Cluster: A set of nodes clustered together.
		3.3 Master: Another node kubernetes installed in it which is responsible for managing the worker nodes.
		3.4 Components: 
			I. etcd: Stores all data used to manage the cluster in a distributed way.
			II. Kubelet: Runs on each node on the cluster like an agent and makes sure the nodes are working as expected
			III. Container runtime: Underlying software used to run containers
			IV. Controller: Controls, manages the worker nodes and makes decions.
			V. Scheduler: Distribute work across nodes like taskmaster
			VI. API server: Frontend for kubernetes, to interact with the cluster
		3.5 Master vs workes nodes: How master and worker nodes are different
			I. Master nodes have the components a master requires api-server, etc, controller, scheduler
			II. Worker nodes have the containerd runtime and kubelet
		3.6 Kubectl: Command line utility
			I. Use to deploy and manage applications on a cluster.
			II. Get cluster and application information
			III. kubectl cluster-info and get nodes.  
	4. Docker vs containerd
		4.1  Docker: Popular container product
			I. Is not just a container runtime alone
			II. It is a complete platform
		4.2  Rkt: Container product which also exists
		4.3  Kubernetes: Started as a tool for managing docker. 
			I. Then as it got more popular, other containerization products wanted to join
			II. So the kubernetes needed to support them as well
			III. They needed to find a way to do that. So they introduced container runtime interface and that allowed for any product that adheres to the OCI to be managed by kubernetes.
			IV. At the and they ditched docker as a platform to use containerd instead.
		4.4  Containerd
			I. runc'yi yönetmekte kullanılan koşma zamanı yöneticisiydi
			II. Zaman içinde ayrı bir proje olarak devam etti 
			III. Tek başına indirilebilir ve crictl ile kullanılabilir
			IV. ctr is for debugging
			V. nerdctl is general purpose like docker
			VI. crictl is used for debugging cri compatible container 
